n use these values.','Field mappings'=>'Field mappings','One mapping per line: LDAP attribute:WordPress meta key:type. Example: %1$s. Types: %2$s or %3$s.'=>'One mapping per line: LDAP attribute:WordPress meta key:type. Example: %1$s. Types: %2$s or %3$s.','Group roles'=>'Group roles','Set the WordPress role from LDAP groups at each login. The first matching rule applies. If no rule matches, use the default role. Recovery accounts and super administrators are excluded.'=>'Set the WordPress role from LDAP groups at each login. The first matching rule applies. If no rule matches, use the default role. Recovery accounts and super administrators are excluded.','Group-to-role rules'=>'Group-to-role rules','One group:role rule per line. Example: Editors:editor. Leave blank to keep current roles.'=>'One group:role rule per line. Example: Editors:editor. Leave blank to keep current roles.','Enterprise includes scheduled account import, scheduled access removal, and multisite membership rules. Your saved settings are kept.'=>'Enterprise includes scheduled account import, scheduled access removal, and multisite membership rules. Your saved settings are kept.','View Enterprise upgrade'=>'View Enterprise upgrade','Enterprise account settings'=>'Enterprise account settings','Multisite membership'=>'Multisite membership','Assign site membership and roles from directory groups. The first matching rule for each site applies. These rules replace the group role rules for network activation.'=>'Assign site membership and roles from directory groups. The first matching rule for each site applies. These rules replace the group role rules for network activation.','Group-to-site rules'=>'Group-to-site rules','One group:site ID:role rule per line. Example: Editors:2:editor. On group removal, restore prior membership or remove a membership created by these rules. Manual role changes are kept on removal. Leave blank to stop membership updates.'=>'One group:site ID:role rule per line. Example: Editors:2:editor. On group removal, restore prior membership or remove a membership created by these rules. Manual role changes are kept on removal. Leave blank to stop membership updates.','Scheduled account import'=>'Scheduled account import','Import directory accounts once per hour through WordPress scheduled tasks. Set a search account on Connection. Site traffic or a system task must run WordPress cron.'=>'Import directory accounts once per hour through WordPress scheduled tasks. Set a search account on Connection. Site traffic or a system task must run WordPress cron.','Enable scheduled import'=>'Enable scheduled import','Create accounts without a first login. Existing local accounts are excluded. No user session is created.'=>'Create accounts without a first login. Existing local accounts are excluded. No user session is created.','Import Base DN'=>'Import Base DN','Leave blank to use the connection Base DN.'=>'Leave blank to use the connection Base DN.','Import groups'=>'Import groups','One group per line. Import users in at least one group. Leave blank to import all users below the Import Base DN. Login group restrictions also apply.'=>'One group per line. Import users in at least one group. Leave blank to import all users below the Import Base DN. Login group restrictions also apply.','Scheduled access removal'=>'Scheduled access removal','Check managed directory accounts once per hour. A confirmed missing account, disabled AD account, changed directory identity, or failed login group rule suspends access and ends all WordPress sessions. Connection errors keep the current access state.'=>'Check managed directory accounts once per hour. A confirmed missing account, disabled AD account, changed directory identity, or failed login group rule suspends access and ends all WordPress sessions. Connection errors keep the current access state.','Enable scheduled access removal'=>'Enable scheduled access removal','Keep user data and content. Restore access after a later successful directory check. Recovery accounts and super administrators are excluded. Existing suspensions remain if the task or license stops.'=>'Keep user data and content. Restore access after a later successful directory check. Recovery accounts and super administrators are excluded. Existing suspensions remain if the task or license stops.','Custom field storage'=>'Custom field storage','Leave the defaults unless your integration uses different user meta keys.'=>'Leave the defaults unless your integration uses different user meta keys.','LDAP value suffix'=>'LDAP value suffix','Stores the LDAP value, such as phone_ldap.'=>'Stores the LDAP value, such as phone_ldap.','WordPress value suffix'=>'WordPress value suffix','Stores the editable WordPress value, such as phone_wp.'=>'Stores the editable WordPress value, such as phone_wp.','Single sign-on (SSO)'=>'Single sign-on (SSO)','Sign users in to WordPress after your web server authenticates them.'=>'Sign users in to WordPress after your web server authenticates them.','Enable single sign-on'=>'Enable single sign-on','Users do not need a second login for WordPress.'=>'Users do not need a second login for WordPress.','Configure your web server to authenticate users and set REMOTE_USER. Enter an LDAP search account on Connection.'=>'Configure your web server to authenticate users and set REMOTE_USER. Enter an LDAP search account on Connection.','Do not copy browser headers into REMOTE_USER. Block access that bypasses web server authentication.'=>'Do not copy browser headers into REMOTE_USER. Block access that bypasses web server authentication.','Web server authentication'=>'Web server authentication','REMOTE_USER is present.'=>'REMOTE_USER is present.','REMOTE_USER is missing. Check the web server configuration.'=>'REMOTE_USER is missing. Check the web server configuration.','An Enterprise license is required to collect, read, or export audit history. Existing records are kept.'=>'An Enterprise license is required to collect, read, or export audit history. Existing records are kept.','Enterprise audit settings'=>'Enterprise audit settings','Audit history'=>'Audit history','Record login results and account changes. Records contain event names and account IDs. Passwords, directory field values, and credentials are excluded.'=>'Record login results and account changes. Records contain event names and account IDs. Passwords, directory field values, and credentials are excluded.','Enable audit history'=>'Enable audit history','Store private WordPress records. Collection is off by default. Existing records remain when collection stops.'=>'Store private WordPress records. Collection is off by default. Existing records remain when collection stops.','Retention (days)'=>'Retention (days)','Default: 30. Range: 1 to 3650. A daily task removes older records while collection is enabled.'=>'Default: 30. Range: 1 to 3650. A daily task removes older records while collection is enabled.','Export CSV'=>'Export CSV','Latest 50 records. The export includes all retained records in this scope. Times use UTC.'=>'Latest 50 records. The export includes all retained records in this scope. Times use UTC.','Time (UTC)'=>'Time (UTC)','Event'=>'Event','Actor ID'=>'Actor ID','User ID'=>'User ID','Site ID'=>'Site ID','You do not have permission to export these records.'=>'You do not have permission to export these records.','Activate an Enterprise license to change these settings. Your saved settings are kept.'=>'Activate an Enterprise license to change these settings. Your saved settings are kept.','A Pro setting is not valid. Check the format and role names.'=>'A Pro setting is not valid. Check the format and role names.','The update was stopped. Activate Simple LDAP Login Pro to restore LDAP login.'=>'The update was stopped. Activate Simple LDAP Login Pro to restore LDAP login.','Update blocked: This package does not include all Pro files. To install Free, deactivate the plugin first. Your installed